 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nMAC Authorization header format is incorrect\n\nWhen using MAC authentication with oauthlib, the Authorization header is being generated with incorrect formatting. According to the MAC Authentication specification, the header values should be separated by spaces, but the current implementation is using commas.\n\nFor example, the current implementation produces:\n\n```\nAuthorization: MAC id=\"token123\",nonce=\"abc123\",mac=\"signature\"\n```\n\nBut the correct format should be:\n\n```\nAuthorization: MAC id=\"token123\" nonce=\"abc123\" mac=\"signature\"\n```\n\nThis causes authentication to fail with servers that strictly follow the MAC Authentication specification.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.tokens import prepare_mac_header\n\n# Example usage\nheaders = prepare_mac_header(\n    token=\"token123\",\n    uri=\"https://example.com/resource\",\n    key=\"secret_key\",\n    http_method=\"GET\",\n    nonce=\"abc123\",\n    hash_algorithm=\"hmac-sha-1\"\n)\n\nprint(headers['Authorization'])\n# Outputs: MAC id=\"token123\",nonce=\"abc123\",mac=\"signature\"\n# Should be: MAC id=\"token123\" nonce=\"abc123\" mac=\"signature\"\n```\n\nThis issue affects all MAC authentication requests made through the library.\n</issue>\n",
 "fixture": {},
